{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said, etc., לֵאמֹר (saying).</b> The verse's saying <b>לֵאמֹר</b> — the meaning is that Moses might think that the statement ״כֵּן בְּנוֹת ״ etc. constitutes the words spoken to Moses, who had presented the case, and there is no need to state them to anyone else; therefore it says ״לֵאמֹר״ — that he should likewise say it to them. And it is possible that it is not to them alone but to Israel, and therefore it did not say ״לֵאמֹר לָהֶם״ (saying to them). Or it is possible that from the fact that it says afterward ״וְאֶל בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ etc., it revealed that what preceded does not need to be said except to the daughters of Tzelofchad; accordingly, the ״לֵאמֹר״ it stated means to say it to the daughters."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:15:21.322895671Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}